## 🛠️ Commandes et Code utiles (Module 2)

**Lancer Kestra en local via Docker :**
```bash
# Téléchargement du fichier docker-compose.yml officiel de Kestra
curl -L https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kestra-io/kestra/main/docker-compose.yml -o docker-compose.yml

# Démarrer Kestra
docker-compose up -d

# Accéder à l'interface UI : http://localhost:8080/ui
```

**Exemple de Flow Kestra (`etl_nyc_taxi.yaml`) :**
```yaml
id: etl_nyc_taxi_to_gcs
namespace: de_zoomcamp_module_2

inputs:
  - id: dataset_url
    type: STRING
    defaults: "https://github.com/DataTalksClub/nyc-tlc-data/releases/download/yellow/yellow_tripdata_2021-01.csv.gz"

tasks:
  - id: download_data
    type: io.kestra.plugin.core.http.Download
    uri: "{{ inputs.dataset_url }}"

  - id: transform_data
    type: io.kestra.plugin.scripts.python.Script
    containerImage: python:3.9-slim
    beforeCommands:
      - pip install pandas pyarrow
    script: |
      import pandas as pd
      import os
      
      # Kestra injecte automatiquement le fichier de la tâche précédente
      input_path = "{{ outputs.download_data.uri }}"
      output_path = "transformed_data.parquet"
      
      df = pd.read_csv(input_path, compression='gzip')
      # Nettoyage basique
      df = df[df['passenger_count'] > 0]
      df.to_parquet(output_path)
      
      # Export pour Kestra
      print(f"::set-output name=output_file::{output_path}")

  - id: upload_to_gcs
    type: io.kestra.plugin.gcp.gcs.Upload
    serviceAccount: "{{ secret('GCP_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON') }}"
    bucket: "de-zoomcamp-bucket-2026"
    from: "{{ outputs.transform_data.vars.output_file }}"
    to: "nyc_taxi/2021-01.parquet"

triggers:
  - id: daily_schedule
    type: io.kestra.plugin.core.trigger.Schedule
    cron: "0 2 * * *"
```

